{"content":[{"c":["LIBNAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of the stations at which the Israelites encamped during the wilderness journey. It was situated between Rimmon-perez and Rissah (",{"href":"?bref=Num.33.20-21","r":"Num.33.20-21","rawR":"Num.33.20-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.33.20-21","value":"Num.33.20-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 33:20-21"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Wilderness Wanderings"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Canaanite city-state in southern Palestine, conquered and destroyed by the Israelites under Joshua (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.10.29-31","r":"Josh.10.29-31","rawR":"Josh.10.29-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.10.29-31","value":"Josh.10.29-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 10:29-31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.12.15","r":"Josh.12.15","rawR":"Josh.12.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.12.15","value":"Josh.12.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:15"},"). It was located within Judah’s territory (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.42","r":"Josh.15.42","rawR":"Josh.15.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.42","value":"Josh.15.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:42"},") and later given to the Levites for an inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.13","r":"Josh.21.13","rawR":"Josh.21.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.13","value":"Josh.21.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.57","r":"1Chr.6.57","rawR":"1Chr.6.57","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.57","value":"1Chr.6.57"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:57"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["Three details in the city’s subsequent history are noted in Scripture: (1) During the reign of King Jehoram of Judah, at the time of Edom’s uprising, Libnah joined in the revolt but was subdued (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.8.22","r":"2Kgs.8.22","rawR":"2Kgs.8.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.8.22","value":"2Kgs.8.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 8:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.21.10","r":"2Chr.21.10","rawR":"2Chr.21.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.21.10","value":"2Chr.21.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 21:10"},"). (2) After King Sennacherib of Assyria took the city of Lachish, he proceeded to attack Libnah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.19.8","r":"2Kgs.19.8","rawR":"2Kgs.19.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.19.8","value":"2Kgs.19.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 19:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.37.8","r":"Isa.37.8","rawR":"Isa.37.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.37.8","value":"Isa.37.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 37:8"},"). Earlier Isaiah had affirmed to King Hezekiah that a rumor would cause the invading king to interrupt his military campaign against Judah and return to his own land; it was while Sennacherib was besieging Libnah that Isaiah’s affirmation was confirmed (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.19.7-8","r":"2Kgs.19.7-8","rawR":"2Kgs.19.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.19.7-8","value":"2Kgs.19.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 19:7-8"},"). (3) The mother of Jehoahaz and Zedekiah, two of Judah’s last kings, was a native of Libnah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.23.31","r":"2Kgs.23.31","rawR":"2Kgs.23.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.23.31","value":"2Kgs.23.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 23:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.24.18","r":"2Kgs.24.18","rawR":"2Kgs.24.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.24.18","value":"2Kgs.24.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"24:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.52.1","r":"Jer.52.1","rawR":"Jer.52.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.52.1","value":"Jer.52.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 52:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Libnah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 33:20-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.33.20-21","rawQueryValue":"Num.33.20-21","sourceRefExact":"Num.33.20-21"},{"anchorText":"Jos 10:29-31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.10.29-31","rawQueryValue":"Josh.10.29-31","sourceRefExact":"Josh.10.29-31"},{"anchorText":"12:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.12.15","rawQueryValue":"Josh.12.15","sourceRefExact":"Josh.12.15"},{"anchorText":"15:42","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.42","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.42","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.42"},{"anchorText":"Jos 21:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.13","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.13","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:57","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.57","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.57","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.57"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 8:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.8.22","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.8.22","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.8.22"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 21:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.21.10","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.21.10","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.21.10"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 19:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.19.8","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.19.8","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.19.8"},{"anchorText":"Is 37:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.37.8","rawQueryValue":"Isa.37.8","sourceRefExact":"Isa.37.8"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 19:7-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.19.7-8","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.19.7-8","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.19.7-8"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 23:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.23.31","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.23.31","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.23.31"},{"anchorText":"24:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.24.18","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.24.18","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.24.18"},{"anchorText":"Jer 52:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.52.1","rawQueryValue":"Jer.52.1","sourceRefExact":"Jer.52.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6739581d37a9890048eef20d4edf1419c674b41eee9c71b36bf95030ee8986ad","sourceItemName":"Libnah","sourceItemOrder":86,"sourceMember":"Articles/L.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Libnah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Libnah","title":"Libnah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}